# Performance Rules

Keep the backend responsive under realistic hospital workloads.

## Requirements
- List endpoints must paginate by default.
- Use narrow `select`/`include` shapes and must not introduce N+1 queries.
- Index hot filter and join columns.
- Move expensive exports, report generation, and reconciliation off the request thread.
- Profile before introducing caches.
- p95 targets should suit staff-facing workflows and be reviewed in readiness checks.
- Post-mutation websocket publishes should stay off the critical HTTP path (fire-and-forget after commit).
- Realtime payloads must stay minimal for instant UI reconciliation without full refetches.
- Entitlement and ABAC recipient resolution for broadcasts must be indexed and cached on hot paths.
